N-Methyl-N-phenyl-4-aminobutyronitrile (348.5 mg, 2 mmol) was treated
with 1M borane/THF (30 ml). The solution was refluxed for 2 h, cooled and
treated with methanol. The solvent was then evaporated in vacuo. The
residue was refluxed with 10% hydrochloric acid (30 ml) for 2 h, filtered
and made alkaline with 10% aqueous sodium hydroxide. The alkaline mixture
was extracted with ethyl acetate (4 × 20 ml). The organic phase was
washed with water (5 ml), dried over sodium sulfate and filtered. The
solvent was evaporated in vacuo and the resulting crude liquid was
purified by column chromatography (silica gel,
dichloromethane:methanol:isopropylamine 10:1:0.1). Yield: 83%, pale
yellow oil.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM overall yield 49% in two steps from
N-Methyl-N-phenyl-4-aminobutyronitrile
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An Efficient Synthesis of N-Alkyl-N-arylputrescines and Cadaverines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mollo, Maria C.; Gruber, Nadia; Diaz, Jimena E.; Bisceglia, Juan A.;
Orelli, Liliana R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2014), 46(5), 444-452

