$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure B: Starting material (100 mg) was dissolved in
acetonitrile (4 mL) and stirred at room temperature. 5 % Pd/C (0.039 g,
1.8 x 10-5 mol) and NH4HCO2 (0.60 g, 9.5 x 10-3 mol) dissolved in H2O
(1.0 mL) was then added to the reaction mixture while stirring. The
reaction was monitored by TLC for the disappearance of the spot lowest
Rf) corresponding to the primary amine intermediate. The reaction mixture
was then filtered, washed successively with methanol and CH2Cl2 and the
filtrate evaporated in vacuo. The residue was dissolved in CH2Cl2 and the
organic layer was separated, dried in Na2SO4 and filtered. The filtrate
was then evaporated in vacuo to give the product.
N-Ethyl-2-methylaniline: Starting from 2-nitrotoluene (0.10 g, 7.3 x 10-4
mol) and using general procedure B gave a clear, colorless liquid (0.081
g, 82.4 %). Rf 0.71 (10:1 hexanes:ethyl acetate); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3,
δH) 1.37 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 2.20 (s, 3H), 3.25 (q, J = 7.2 Hz , 2H),
6.67-6.74 (m, 2H), 7.12 (d, 1H), 7.18-7.22 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3, δC) 15.3, 17.8, 38.7, 109.9, 117.0; 122.0, 127.4, 130.29, 146.7;
GCMS (EI) m/z 135.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reductive monoalkylation of aromatic and aliphatic nitro compounds and
the corresponding amines with nitriles
