$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-((3R,4R)-2,4-dimethyl-3-phenyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroisoquinolin-4-yl)ethanamine
(7)- A flame dried 25 mL round bottom flask was cooled under argon before
being charged with 2a (70.0 mg, 0.241 mmol, 1 equiv), and freshly
distilled THF (8 mL). The resulting solution was cooled to 0 °C before
having LiAlH4 added in one portion (182 mg, 4.82 mmol, 20 equiv). This
suspension was stirred at this temperature for 30 minutes before being
warmed to room temperature where it was stirred for an addition 30
minutes. The reaction was then fitted with an oven dried reflux condenser
and the reaction was heated to reflux for 18 hours at which time TLC
analysis indicated clean and full conversion of starting material. The
reaction was cooled to 0 °C and water (1 mL) was added drop wise. The
reaction was warmed to room temperature and its volume was doubled with a
saturated aqueous solution of Rochelle’s salt and EtOAc (15 mL) was
added. The resulting emulsion was stirred vigorously for 30 minutes at
which time clean phase separation was evident. The layers were separated
and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (2x). The combined organic
layers were washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude diamine was purified using Si gel flash
column chromatography using EtOAc:MeOH:NH4OH (25:25:1 v:v:v) as the as
the mobile phase. The title compound was isolated as a clear and light
yellow oil (56.3 mg, 0.201 mmol, 83%). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.35-7.16 (m, 6H), 7.15-7.11 (m, 2H), 7.08-7.03 (m, 1H), 3.79 (d, J =
16.0 Hz, 1H), 3.64 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H), 3.41 (s, 1H), 2.73-2.62 (m, 1H),
2.55-2.46 (m, 1H), 2.22 (s(br), 2H), 2.16 (s, 3H), 2.14-2.07 (m, 1H),
1.55-1.46 (m, 1H), 1.31 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 142.06,
136.02, 133.97, 130.42, 127.62, 127.18, 126.46, 126.05, 125.76, 125.73,
74.83, 56.30, 44.20, 41.67, 40.86, 37.89, 28.80. IR (cm-1, film) 3362,
2953, 2775, 1581, 1491, 1452, 1375, 1251. HRMS (ESI): Calc’d for
C19H25N2, 281.20177; found, 281.20181. The enantiomeric purity of this
compound was not determined by HPLC. [α] D 20 -54.0 (c = 0.2, CHCl3).
