$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the preparation of
homoallylic amines by one-potallylboration of aromatic and
fluoro-benzonitriles (7a-7e and 7h-7k) :(S)-1-phenylbut-3-en-1-amine: To
a solution of benzonitrile (300mg, 2.9 mmol) in diethyl ether (5 ml)
lithium triethylborohydride (2; 1 M in THF;2.9 mL, 2.9 mmol) was added at
0 °C and the solution was stirred for 2 h. Methanol (92mg, 2.9 mmol) was
added to the reaction mixture and stirred for 30 minutes. The
reactionmixture was cooled to -100 °C and slowly transferred to via
canula to a stirring solutionpre cooledto -100 °C and diluted with ether.
After 6 h, the reaction mixture was slowlywarmed to -78 °C and stirring
was continued for 16 h more. Then the reaction mixturewas oxidised very
slowly with NaOH (3 M in H2O; 1.2 mL) and H2O2 (30% in H2O; 1.2mL) and
was left stirring overnight under positive N2 pressure while it slowly
warmed toroom temperature. The product was then extracted with Et2O (3X30
mL), the combinedorganic layer was washed with saturated brine solution
and dried over anhy. Na2SO4.Next, the solvent was evaporated under
reduced pressure, and the crude product waspurified on silica gel
(hexanes:ethyl acetate:triethylamine 84.5:15:0.5) to afford product.
(S)-1-(thiophen-2-yl)but-3-en-1-amine. Yield 82%. 7.19-7.16 (m,
1H),6.96-6.92 (m, 2H), 5.89-5.68 (m,1H), 5.18-5.09 (m, 2H), 4.27 (dd,
J=7.6 Hz, J=5.4 Hz,1H), 2.64-2.34 (m, 2H), 1.69 (br s, 2H); 13C NMR: (75
MHz, CDCl3)δ 150.8, 135.1,126.9, 123.9, 123.1, 118.6, 52.3, 45.8.
