$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of phenyl magnesium bromide prepared from bromobenzene
(5.32 g, 33.9 mmol) and magnesium turnings (0.84 g, 34.7 mmol) in diethyl
ether (50 mL) was added the nitrile (2.20 g, 27.12 mmol) at room
temperature, with the resulting mixture being refluxed for 4 h. After
cool, anhydrous MeOH (1.37ml, 33.9 mmol) was added (vigorous reaction)
and the reaction stirred for 1h, followed by addition of LiAlH4 (1.54g,
40.7 mmol). The reaction was stirred overnight and quenched with the
careful addition of water (10 mL) with the organic layer being decanted.
The residue was washed with diethyl ether (2 x 30 mL), the ether layers
were combined, washed with 10 % aqueous sodium bicarbonate, dried over
MgSO4 and the solvent removed in vacuo to yield the crude product (3.50
g, 80%). The latter was purified by bulb-to-bulb distillation to give the
product as a clear colourless oil. 1H NMR (C6D6, 298K, 400 MHz) 0.95
(broad s, 2H), 1.58-1.67 (m, 2H), 1.90-2.06 (m, 2H), 3.67 (t, 1H, J = 6.8
Hz), 4.98 (apparent d, 1H, J = 10.2 Hz), 5.00 (apparent d, 1H, J =16.9
Hz), 5.75 (ddt, 1H, J = 16.9, 10.2, 6.8 Hz), 7.04-7.15 (m, 5H); 13C NMR
(C6D6, 298K, 100 MHz) 31.0, 39.3, 55.9, 114.7, 126.8, 127.0, 128.5,
138.8, 147.4. [Lit.13 1H NMR (CDCl3, 298K, 400 MHz) 1.45 (broad s, 2H),
1.75 (m, 2H), 2.04 (m, 2H), 3.89 (t, 1H, J = 6.9 Hz), 4.93-5.03 (m, 2H),
5.80 (m, 1H), 7.23 (m, 1H), 7.31 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 298K, 100 MHz)
30.7, 38.6, 55.6, 114.7, 126.3, 126.9, 128.4, 138.2, 146.4].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in-situ generated reactant
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Intramolecular Hydroamination of Aminoalkenes by Calcium and Magnesium
Complexes: A Synthetic and Mechanistic Study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Crimmin, Mark R.; Arrowsmith, Merle; Barrett, Anthony G. M.; Casely, Ian
J.; Hill, Michael S.; Procopiou, Panayiotis A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2009), 131(28), 9670-9685

