$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the preparation of homoallylic amines by
one-potallylboration of aromatic and fluoro-benzonitriles (7a-7e and
7h-7k) :(S)-1-phenylbut-3-en-1-amine: To a solution of benzonitrile
(300mg, 2.9 mmol) in diethyl ether (5 ml) lithium triethylborohydride (2;
1 M in THF;2.9 mL, 2.9 mmol) was added at 0 °C and the solution was
stirred for 2 h. Methanol (92mg, 2.9 mmol) was added to the reaction
mixture and stirred for 30 minutes. The reactionmixture was cooled to
-100 °C and slowly transferred to via canula to a stirring solutionpre
cooledto -100 °C and diluted with ether. After 6 h, the reaction mixture
was slowlywarmed to -78 °C and stirring was continued for 16 h more. Then
the reaction mixturewas oxidised very slowly with NaOH (3 M in H2O; 1.2
mL) and H2O2 (30% in H2O; 1.2mL) and was left stirring overnight under
positive N2 pressure while it slowly warmed toroom temperature. The
product was then extracted with Et2O (3X30 mL), the combinedorganic layer
was washed with saturated brine solution and dried over anhy.
Na2SO4.Next, the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure, and the
crude product waspurified on silica gel (hexanes:ethyl
acetate:triethylamine 84.5:15:0.5) to afford product. Yield 336 mg2.29
mmol, 79%. 1H NMR: (300 MHz, CDCl3)δ 7.37-7.22 (m, 5H), 5.82-5.69 (m,
1H),5.15-5.07 (m, 2H), 4.00 (t, J=8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.50-2.32 (m, 2H), 1.59
(br s, 2H); 13C NMR:(75 MHz, CDCl3)δ 146.0, 135.7, 128.7, 127.3, 126.6,
118.1, 56.4, 45.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Convenient Synthesis of Stable Aldimine-Borane Complexes, Chiral δ-Amino
Alcohols, and γ-Substituted GABA Analogues from Nitriles
