$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure A mixture of ketone (10
mmol), aldehyde (10 mmol), nitrile (10 mmol), anhydrous ZnCl2 (4.08 g, 30
mmol), and CH2Cl2 (20 mL) as solvent was stirred with exclusion of
moisture at 25°C for 10 min. Tetrachlorosilane (3.6 mL, 30 mmol) was then
added, and the reaction mixture was stirred again for the specified time.
The reaction mixture was poured onto ice cold water (100 mL), neutralized
with Na2CO3 solution, and extracted with CHCl3 (2 x 50 mL). The extract
was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and the solvent was removed by
distillation. Finally the residue was purified by chromatographic methods
to obtain the pure products.
N-[3-Oxo-1-phenyl-3-(thien-2-yl)propyl]benzamide (2a), yield 78%. M.p.:
115°C. Rf = 0.45 (PE/AcOEt 2:1). IR: ν 3280 (NH), 3080-3030 (CH, Ar),
2922-2860 (CH2. CH), 1658 (C=O), 1642 (CONH), 1600, 1545, 1515 (C=C,Ar)
cm-1. 1H-NMR: δ 6.82-7.78 (m, 14H, ArH+NH), 5.29(q, 1H, CH), 3.64 (dd, 3J
= 5 Hz, 2J = 16.1 Hz, 1H, CH2), 3.34 (dd, 3J = 5.6 Hz, 2J = 16.1 Hz, 1H,
CH2). MS: m/z (%) 335 (M+, 16),230 (M+ -COPh, 25.5), 111 (thenoyl, 80),
105 (COPh, 100). Anal. Calcd. for C20H17NO2S (335.42): C, 71.62; H, 5.11;
N, 4.18; S, 9.56. Found: C, 71.60; H, 5.80; N, 3.95; S, 9.52%.
