$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure for Formation of Amine 8 To a flame dried Schlenk tube
containing a magnetic stirring bar were added triphenylacetonitrile 6aaa
(26.9 mg, 0.1 mmol), 2-propanol (2 mL), Raney nickel (0.2 g taken from
Raney nickel stored in 2-propanol), and KOH (100 mg). A condenser was
fixed onto the flask and the mixture was refluxed with stirring at 100 °C
for 48 h. After cooling to room temperature, 1M HClaq (2 mL) was added
and the reaction mixture was stirred for 30 min at room temperature. Then
5M NaOHaq (3 mL) and benzoyl chloride (58.6 μL, 0.5 mmol) were added to
the reaction mixture and the resulting mixture stirred at room
temperature for 6 h. The mixture was diluted with water (2 mL) and
extracted with EtOAc (3 ×15 mL). The combined organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product
was purified by PTLC (EtOAc/hexane = 5:95).
N-(2,2,2-triphenylethyl)benzamide 8aaa (29 mg, 77%) as a white solid. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.64 (d, J = 5.6 Hz, 2H), 5.74 (br.s, 1H),
7.23-7.42 (m, 20H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 48.2, 57.1, 126.6, 126.8,
128.4, 128.5, 129.0, 131.4, 134.4, 145.1, 166.9. IR (Neat) ν 671, 698,
714, 751, 759, 801, 1029, 1272, 1444, 1482, 1510, 1659, 3047, 3059 cm-1.
HRMS (DART) m/z calcd for C27H24NO [M+H]+: 378.1852, found 378.1850.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Raney nickel used
